e=\"line-height:0px;font-size:0px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;\"><![endif]-->\n    \n      \n      <div style=\"background:#ffffff;background-color:#ffffff;margin:0px auto;border-radius:0px;max-width:600px;\">\n        \n        <table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"background:#ffffff;background-color:#ffffff;width:100%;border-radius:0px;\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n              <td style=\"direction:ltr;font-size:0px;padding:20px 0;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;padding-top:10px;text-align:center;\">\n                <!--[if mso | IE]><table role=\"presentation\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td class=\"\" style=\"vertical-align:top;width:560px;\" ><![endif]-->\n            \n      <div class=\"mj-column-per-100 mj-outlook-group-fix\" style=\"font-size:0px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;\">\n        \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0px;\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"width:400px;\">\n              \n      <img height=\"auto\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/msgsndr/oKvxmpgImkZb3TwM9ii4/media/667c7b5ab458d55a15346991.jpeg\" style=\"border:0;display:block;outline:none;text-decoration:none;height:auto;width:100%;font-size:13px;\" width=\"400\">\n    \n            </td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n          </tbody>\n\n        </table>\n    \n            </td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    \n      </div>\n    \n          <!--[if mso | IE]></td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        \n      </div>\n    \n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]></td></tr></table><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"width:600px;\" width=\"600\" bgcolor=\"#ffffff\" ><tr><td style=\"line-height:0px;font-size:0px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;\"><![endif]-->\n    \n      \n      <div style=\"background:#ffffff;background-color:#ffffff;margin:0px auto;border-radius:0px;max-width:600px;\">\n        \n        <table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"background:#ffffff;background-color:#ffffff;width:100%;border-radius:0px;\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n              <td style=\"direction:ltr;font-size:0px;padding:20px 0;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;padding-top:10px;text-align:center;\">\n                <!--[if mso | IE]><table role=\"presentation\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td class=\"\" style=\"vertical-align:top;width:560px;\" ><![endif]-->\n            \n      <div class=\"mj-column-per-100 mj-outlook-group-fix\" style=\"font-size:0px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;\">\n        \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <p style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:100%;\">\n      </p>\n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:520px;\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"520px\" ><tr><td style=\"height:0;line-height:0;\"> &nbsp;\n</td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n    \n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr><tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><h2 style=\"margin-top: 14pt;margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The 7 Things You Must Check in a Purchase Agreement Before Buying an Accounting Firm</span></h2><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hi Sara,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you\u2019re buying an accounting practice, you\u2019re going to come across a purchase agreement\u2014and let\u2019s be real, it will probably look like a 20-page legal maze designed to put you to sleep. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">But here\u2019s the thing: this document controls everything about your deal. It\u2019s your business\u2019s user manual, your playbook, and, if something goes wrong, your only protection.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">So today, I\u2019m breaking down the seven key sections you <em>must</em> understand before signing on the dotted line.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>1. What Exactly Are You Buying? (And What\u2019s Excluded?)</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This is where you find out if you\u2019re getting <strong>all</strong> the assets you expect\u2014or if the seller conveniently forgot to include key client lists, software, or equipment. If you\u2019re the buyer, you want the contract to say <em>everything</em> is included <em>unless</em> specifically excluded. If you\u2019re the seller? You want the opposite.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>2. The Money Details (a.k.a. The Purchase Price)</strong></span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">How much are you paying?</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Is it all cash, or is there a promissory note?</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Are there any earnout term or price adjustments based on client retention or revenue?</span></p></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Miss something here, and you might be in for a nasty surprise later.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>3. Closing Mechanics: When Does This Deal Actually Happen?</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Most deals aren\u2019t \u201csign today, close today.\u201d They involve a bifurcated sign-and-close, meaning:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">\u2714 You sign the agreement now.<br>\u2714 The deal officially closes later\u2014after financing, approvals, or other conditions are met.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you don\u2019t structure this properly, you could be legally obligated to buy before securing funding. (Yes, I\u2019ve seen this happen. Yes, it got ugly.)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>4. The Seller\u2019s Promises (And Why They Matter)</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Reps and warranties are the seller\u2019s legal promises about the business. Things like:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">\u201cOur financial statements are accurate.\u201d</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">\u201cWe actually own the assets we\u2019re selling.\u201d</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">\u201cWe haven\u2019t secretly sold the client list to someone else.\u201d</span></p></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If any of these turn out to be false, you\u2019ve got a breach of contract claim. But only if you made sure they were included in writing. These are SUPER important.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>5. What Happens If Something Goes Wrong?</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This is where indemnification comes in\u2014it decides who pays if a lawsuit shows up later.</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-inline-start:48px;\"><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Example: A client sues over work done <em>before</em> closing.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Who\u2019s responsible\u2014you or the seller?</span></p></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Get this section wrong, and you could be on the hook for past problems you had nothing to do with.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>6. Non-Compete Clauses (The Fine Print That Matters)</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you\u2019re the buyer, you don\u2019t want the seller setting up shop across the street and poaching clients. If you\u2019re the seller, you don\u2019t want to be banned from your entire profession for the next decade.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The right non-compete is a balance\u2014clear, enforceable, and <em>specific</em>. If it\u2019s too broad, courts might throw it out. If it\u2019s too narrow, it won\u2019t protect you. If you\u2019re the one under a non-compete, you\u2019re going to want it to be specific enough that you can tell whether or not a business opportunity will violate it.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>7. The Boilerplate (Yes, You Still Have to Read It)</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The last section might seem like legal fluff, but I\u2019ve found some wild clauses buried in here\u2014like secret fees, weird assignment rules, and even clauses that completely contradict earlier sections. So read it.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>The Bottom Line</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">A purchase agreement is more than just paperwork\u2014it\u2019s the foundation of your deal. If you don\u2019t understand what\u2019s in it, you\u2019re flying blind.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you\u2019re buying an accounting firm and want to make sure your agreement is airtight, </span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/262d3a27808?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px; color: #3425db !important\">check out our courses at Deal Academy to get the support you need.</span></a></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This is what I do every day, and trust me\u2014you don\u2019t want to find out what\u2019s <em>missing</em> in your contract when it\u2019s already too late.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">To smarter deals,<br>Sara Sharp<br>Partner, SK&amp;S Law Group<br>Business Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy</span></p><p><strong><em>P.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, </em></strong><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/c3b5756e267?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\"><strong><em>fill out this form here</em></strong></span></a><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\"><strong><em>.</em></strong></span></p></div>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr><tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n   